WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:03.199
Hey Vsauce, Daniel here

00:00:03.199 --> 00:00:06.740
What is Vsauce?

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:12.230
Vsauce is a popular educational YouTube channel
helmed by Michael Stevens, or Vsauce Michael,

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:16.940
or that guy who’s always doing the eyebrow
things.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.440
But the whole time I was there I thought a lot about video

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.900
I can do it
I can do it

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:31.490
He looks a little like this, and a bit like
this, and has a personal YouTube channel named

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.020
pooplicker888.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:37.860
But he doesn’t use that anymore.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:43.129
It turns out that there’s a lot of things
that Vsauce isn’t anymore.

00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:49.490
If we assume for a second that Vsauce is what
it is, then Vsauce is a show called Mind Field,

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:54.949
a YouTube premium edutainment show exploring
pop psychology in a professional broadcast

00:00:54.949 --> 00:00:56.470
half hour format.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:01.220
In any given episode Michael will explore
a scientific subject, typically in the realm

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:07.280
of psychology with a particular focus on the
science of perception.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:13.440
We learned that there's a stark difference between what people think they would do and wha they actually do

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.700
The videos are neatly structured into seasons
and episodes with a clear central thesis and

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.170
tight, consistent branding.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:26.870
It isn’t just built like television, it
looks, feels, and sounds like television,

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:31.450
right down to the fabrication of conflict
in a build up to where the commercial breaks

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.500
would go.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:39.980
This forms an interesting contrast between
Vsauce and another similar channel, Vsauce.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.620
Vsauce is a popular educational YouTube channel
helmed by Michael Stevens.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:50.530
In a given video Michael will pop up and for
about ten minutes take the viewer on a pinball

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:55.110
exploration of a scientific subject, typically
in the realm of psychology with a particular

00:01:55.110 --> 00:02:01.940
focus on the science of perception, but also
a fascination with math and astronomy.

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:07.159
A critic of Vsauce might describe the format
of a Vsauce video as “unfocused” with

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:12.850
each video taking its subject matter less
as a thesis and more as an excuse to ramble

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:16.680
for several minutes about vaguely related
subjects.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:23.650
A proponent of Vsauce might describe the format
of a Vsauce video as poetic, with each video

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:28.660
taking its subject matter less as a thesis
and more as a theme, an opportunity to create

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:33.320
a freeform association between ideas that
share a commonality of language

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:37.000
or an overlap of consequences.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:42.120
The video What is the Speed of Dark is less
about the physics of photons and more about

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:50.599
a variety of subjects that all share an intersection
in the idea communicated in the word “dark.”

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:55.860
This unstructured science poetry forms an
interesting contrast between Vsauce and another

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:59.220
similar channel, Vsauce.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.980
Vsauce is a popular variety YouTube channel
helmed by Michael Stevens.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:08.250
In a given video Michael will compile a rapid-fire
freeform presentation assembled around a common

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:14.890
seed idea, like funny or interesting images
or bizarre consumer products, a format riddled

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:18.750
with innuendo, dick jokes, and cleavage.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:23.260
The average Vsauce video will skip across
a couple dozen examples in only a few minutes,

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:28.200
each beat connected to the next by pun or
some other free-association word game with

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:35.760
a particular love for juvenile humour, curious
facts, and optical illusions.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.760
this is the last thing you will see before you die

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.080
can you find the cat?

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.000
But we should move on to girls, in costume, tied up, can you save them?

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.280
This collection of curiosities and innuendo
forms an interesting contrast between Vsauce

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.240
and another similar channel, Vsauce.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:03.250
Vsauce is a popular gaming YouTube channel
helmed by Michael Stevens.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:07.080
In a given video Mark, Michael, Danielle,
Chad, Jeff, and/or Angie will perform stand

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:11.280
up comedy, list video game features, compile
easter eggs, make dick jokes,

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.319
or all of the above.

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:17.769
Whether it’s interesting places in World
of Warcraft, rocks in World of Warcraft that

00:04:17.769 --> 00:04:22.190
look like dicks, or jokes about characters
in World of Warcraft posed in sexually suggestive

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:26.089
positions, you can find it on Vsauce.

00:04:26.089 --> 00:04:27.840
But that’s not all.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.379
Did I mention the standup comedy?

00:04:30.379 --> 00:04:31.460
Yes.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:36.160
You as Dr. Mario are actually working at a free clinic for the members of Jersey Shore!

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.160
Yeah, each level is one of the members of Jersey Shore. The last level? Snookie.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:42.160
It's covered in viruses

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:46.400
This is, in part, the fascinating semantic
language of YouTube.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:51.120
The word “channel” for YouTube is borrowed
from television where a channel is synonymous

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:56.080
with a station, and is largely stationary.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.029
A television station is a fixed point, a portal
through which the viewer watches a flow of

00:05:01.029 --> 00:05:04.110
content as it moves past.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:12.640
A YouTube channel, on the other hand, is less
like this channel and more like this channel.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:18.439
The common metaphor here is flow. A channel
is a means of transport, a space that things

00:05:18.439 --> 00:05:23.860
pass through, but a YouTube channel isn’t
a fixed point, a bench on which you watch

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:28.720
the boats as they sail past, it’s the whole
thing.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.600
You can go to a YouTube channel and walk along
the metaphorical bank by scrolling

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.080
all the way down.

00:05:36.099 --> 00:05:40.059
You can travel from here to here.

00:05:40.059 --> 00:05:45.180
Ludwig Wittgenstein argued that language was
representational, that there is a single factual

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:49.180
reality and it is the job of language to describe
these facts.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:53.800
Language, thus, is like taking a picture,
and the better a language the stronger its

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:58.569
underlying logic, the clearer the picture.

00:05:58.569 --> 00:06:03.309
This brings up an interesting contrast between
the work of Ludwig Wittgenstein and the work

00:06:03.309 --> 00:06:05.729
of Ludwig Wittgenstein.

00:06:05.729 --> 00:06:10.749
Wittgenstein argued that the picture theory
of language was entirely wrong, that words

00:06:10.749 --> 00:06:17.659
are not facts, are not fixed points in space, but rather
words are how you use them.

00:06:17.659 --> 00:06:21.650
In other words use dictates meaning.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:25.529
We have told the story backwards, and now
let us tell it forwards.

00:06:25.529 --> 00:06:31.099
Vsauce, launched in 2010, was a gaming channel
that featured a broad swath of video game

00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:37.199
based dick jokes and boob thumbnails that
morphed into a variety channel compiling interesting

00:06:37.199 --> 00:06:43.899
videos, images, and curiosities, with a particular
focus on dick jokes and boob thumbnails.

00:06:43.899 --> 00:06:49.689
As more and more videos were produced the
curiosities floated to the top until Vsauce

00:06:49.689 --> 00:06:55.920
posted its first self-contained educational
video in July 2011 on the nature

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.520
of explosions.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.640
Hey, Vsauce, Michael here and today I'm in my apartment

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:03.840
Okay, look, the point is that today we're going to talk about explosives.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:09.280
The rapid-fire delivery remained, but the
innuendo gradually took a back seat to questions

00:07:09.309 --> 00:07:14.729
like why the earth has a moon and the existentialism
of atomic physics.

00:07:14.729 --> 00:07:20.560
In September 2012 the last of the variety
shows was posted with Lüt episode 27:

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.229
Carrot Sharpener.

00:07:22.229 --> 00:07:28.210
It is, most likely, this phase here that most
people think of when they say Vsauce.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:32.340
This is when they attracted most of their
14 million subscribers, this is when Bill

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.680
Nye made a guest appearance.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:41.849
Flash forward to January 2017, Vsauce announced
the new, premium show Mind Field available

00:07:41.849 --> 00:07:44.490
only to YouTube Red subscribers.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:49.099
While a few monologue-driven videos have been
released since then, the last of them,

00:07:49.099 --> 00:07:53.610
Which Way Is Down?, was posted in November
2017.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:59.999
As we stand now in February 2019, here on
the bank of Vsauce channel, it looks like

00:07:59.999 --> 00:08:04.119
Mind Field is Vsauce.

00:08:04.119 --> 00:08:08.240
But that’s not the all of it, because that
is simply from now.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:15.539
There is conceivably a future snapshot of
Vsauce where Mind Field is itself just a stratum,

00:08:15.539 --> 00:08:21.460
a phase the channel went through, in the same
way the Vsauce people conceptualize, the freeform

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:27.300
sci-poetry, is a stratum between Mind Field
and the hodgepodge of nonsense and dongs that

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:33.820
preceded it, the same as Lüt and IMG are
a stratum between existential psychology and

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:38.160
painfully dated jokes about Snookie having
sexually transmitted infections.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.680
The last level? Snookie.
It's covered in viruses.

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:50.560
There is no real, essential, elemental Vsauce,
because they are all Vsauce.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:53.600
And as always thanks for watching.

